1
00:00:00,301 --> 00:00:02,891
(Elizabeth:)But then, I remembered
that I'd written it on my hand.

2
00:00:03,637 --> 00:00:06,847
Lucky I didn't confuse it with
what I'd written on my other hand...

3
00:00:07,016 --> 00:00:09,306
(Elizabeth:)...which are the coordinates
for a neutron star.

4
00:00:09,477 --> 00:00:13,477
Because if I tried to go there,
I'd be crushed by hypergravity.

5
00:00:13,689 --> 00:00:15,649
(Elizabeth:)-Anyway, hello.
-Hello.

6
00:00:15,858 --> 00:00:18,988
(Elizabeth:)-Nice to finally meet you in person.
-I would imagine it is.

7
00:00:21,947 --> 00:00:24,737
(Sheldon:)This is my friend and roommate,
Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

8
00:00:24,909 --> 00:00:26,449
(Leonard:)Hi-lo.

9
00:00:27,703 --> 00:00:31,083
(Leonard:)Oops. I started to say hi, and then
I switched to hello in the middle.

10
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:33,128
It came out "hi-lo."

11
00:00:34,377 --> 00:00:35,707
(Leonard:)Duh.

12
00:00:35,878 --> 00:00:38,258
(Leonard:)It's nice to meet you.

13
00:00:38,464 --> 00:00:40,674
(Leonard:)I've read both your books
and your papers.

14
00:00:40,883 --> 00:00:44,473
(Leonard:)I'm Leonard.
I live here. You're brilliant.

15
00:00:44,678 --> 00:00:48,018
(Sheldon:)I apologize.
He's only an experimental physicist.

16
00:00:48,724 --> 00:00:52,264
(Elizabeth:)No need to apologize. Some of my
best friends are experimental physicists.

17
00:00:52,937 --> 00:00:55,107
(Elizabeth:)Well, not my best friends.
But I know them.

18
00:00:56,524 --> 00:00:59,024
(Elizabeth:)My best friend
is a molecular chemist named Wendy.

